esume.rs` | `provider_record_subcommands`, `provider_record_subcommand`, `assert_no_forbidden_provider_subcommands`, `provider_subcommand_is_allowed` | `accessor`, `validator`, `predicate` | Verify the external resume path did not invoke rotation, migration, or legacy resume subcommands. |\n218: \n219: ## Adapter declarations\n220: \n221: ```yaml\n222: adapter_declarations:\n223:   - component: crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs\n224:     role: adapter\n225:     Translates:\n226:       - external provider JSON protocol envelopes\n227:       - Oulipoly typed provider client DTOs\n228:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs\n229:     role: adapter\n230:     Translates:\n231:       - Oulipoly model/provider dispatch context\n232:       - external provider policy.evaluate and launch request JSON contracts\n233:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs\n234:     role: adapter\n235:     Translates:\n236:       - external provider LaunchExit event stream/session metadata\n237:       - Oulipoly runtime execution result and session capture fields\n238:   - component: src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs\n239:     role: adapter\n240:     Translates:\n241:       - Oulipoly resolved resume targets\n242:       - external provider start-known-session launch requests\n243:       - legacy CLI resume requests when no provider ref is present\n244:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs\n245:     role: adapter\n246:     Translates:\n247:       - mailbox session_runtime metadata\n248:       - resume workspace root decisions\n249: ```\n250: \n251: ## Intrinsic-surface declarations\n252: \n253: ```yaml\n254: intrinsic_surface_declarations:\n255:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_registry/options.rs\n256:     role: intrinsic-surface\n257:     Domain: provider_artifact_resolution_options\n258:     Owns:\n259:       - process PATH entry capture for binary provider refs\n260:       - absent PATH handling as an empty resolver entry set\n261:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs\n262:     role: intrinsic-surface\n263:     Domain: external_session_runtime_workspace_root\n264:     Owns:\n265:       - session_runtime.effective_cwd lookup\n266:       - absolute-path validation for recorded external runtime cwd\n267:   - component: src-tauri/src/run/balancing/finalization.rs\n268:     role: intrinsic-surface\n269:     Domain: external_session_runtime_recording\n270:     Owns:\n271:       - non-fatal recording of external provider session runtime cwd\n272: ```\n273: \n274: No other intrinsic surfaces are declared for this gate.\n275: \n276: ## Test-harness declarations\n277: \n278: ```yaml\n279: test_harness_declarations:\n280:   - component: src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs\n281:     role: test-harness\n282:     Surface:\n283:       - isolated XDG config/data/cache fixture directories\n284:       - external provider Python script fixture\n285:       - CLI launch and resume command execution\n286:       - provider request JSONL recording\n287:       - state.db invocation row assertions through rusqlite\n288:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/s10_external_launch_session.rs\n289:     role: test-harness\n290:     Surface:\n291:       - external provider executor service fixture\n292:       - policy.evaluate and launch request capture\n293:       - LaunchExit session capture assertions\n294:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs\n295:     role: test-harness\n296:     Surface:\n297:       - provider artifact registry fixture\n298:       - temporary PATH and executable binary fixture\n299:       - missing artifact diagnostics\n300:   - component: crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs\n301:     role: test-harness\n302:     Surface:\n303:       - provider client subprocess fixture\n304:       - describe response JSON compatibility assertions\n305: ```\n306: \n307: No `state.db` schema migration is declared or required by this gate.\n\n(End of file - total 307 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# s10b Gate Contract\n\n## Component declared roles\n\nComponent: external provider S10 cutover compatibility and resume continuity.\n\nDeclared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\n\nTouched files in scope:\n\n| File | Declared roles | Role notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider client error surface; exposes typed provider-reported process status, parses provider error envelopes, classifies envelopes, and formats stable error text. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider protocol DTO surface; maps provider JSON into typed host protocol structures, parses fixed protocol fields, validates protocol discriminators, and formats protocol strings/errors. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `validator` | Provider client invoke fixture and assertions for describe DTO compatibility, request construction, and fixture environment formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `mapper`, `predicate` | External LaunchExit event/session extraction, non-empty session-id filtering, and runtime result/session capture mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/policy_transform.rs` | `mapper`, `predicate`, `validator` | Applies provider policy transforms to launch candidates while preserving inherited launch environment after acceptance validation and prompt-match checks. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper` | Builds policy and launch protocol requests from runtime provider/model dispatch context, including base-arg filtering and request/working-directory formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_registry/options.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper` | Provider artifact resolver options, including process `PATH` entry derivation. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_settings/mod.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `validator` | Provider settings host options wrapper, registry construction options, cache reads, settings validation, and typed provider/client process-status mapping. |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md","text":"# s10b Gate Contract\n\n## Component declared roles\n\nComponent: external provider S10 cutover compatibility and resume continuity.\n\nDeclared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\n\nTouched files in scope:\n\n| File | Declared roles | Role notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider client error surface; exposes typed provider-reported process status, parses provider error envelopes, classifies envelopes, and formats stable error text. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider protocol DTO surface; maps provider JSON into typed host protocol structures, parses fixed protocol fields, validates protocol discriminators, and formats protocol strings/errors. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `validator` | Provider client invoke fixture and assertions for describe DTO compatibility, request construction, and fixture environment formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `mapper`, `predicate` | External LaunchExit event/session extraction, non-empty session-id filtering, and runtime result/session capture mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/policy_transform.rs` | `mapper`, `predicate`, `validator` | Applies provider policy transforms to launch candidates while preserving inherited launch environment after acceptance validation and prompt-match checks. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper` | Builds policy and launch protocol requests from runtime provider/model dispatch context, including base-arg filtering and request/working-directory formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_registry/options.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper` | Provider artifact resolver options, including process `PATH` entry derivation. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_settings/mod.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `validator` | Provider settings host options wrapper, registry construction options, cache reads, settings validation, and typed provider/client process-status mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Resume workspace-root metadata resolution, including mailbox-backed external session runtime cwd lookup, metadata parsing, and absolute-cwd validation. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider registry fixture, source guards, binary-resolution assertions, request parsing, fixture construction, and helper predicates/filters. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_settings_host.rs` | `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider settings host fixture, structured error/status assertions, provider-call parsing, subcommand filtering, and fixture script formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/s10_external_launch_session.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `validator` | External provider executor fixture proving launch/policy/session protocol shape through fixture construction, request parsing, filtering, and assertions. |\n| `src-tauri/src/app_state.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | GUI app-state construction, service orchestration, path access, and provider registry options construction. |\n| `src-tauri/src/commands/provider_settings.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider settings command host options construction, command orchestration, legacy TOML packaging/parsing, DTO/error mapping, and command validation. |\n| `src-tauri/src/commands/session_locate_export/orchestration.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `validator` | Session locate/export orchestration, environment loading, provider registry construction, output writing, and error/exit mapping. |\n| `src-tauri/src/run/balancing/finalization.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | Completed attempt finalization, artifact/session ingestion, external-session filtering, external session id access, and runtime cwd recording. |\n| `src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `predicate`, `validator` | Headless resume target preparation, provider-ref resume execution, target validation, migration filtering, provider-ref predicates, and failure formatting. |\n| `src-tauri/src/wiring.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | Production and CLI default service graph construction, runtime path mapping, config loading, and directory error formatting. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/age244_s7b_production_wiring_source_guard.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `validator` | Source guard proving production registry constructors use process `PATH` entries through source reads, marker parsing, compact mapping, and assertions. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Full CLI launch/resume fixture proving external provider resume continuity through fixture construction, command orchestration, record parsing/filtering, predicates, and persisted invocation row assertions. |\n\n## Production function inventory\n\nOnly added or meaningfully changed production functions and production DTOs are listed.\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs`\n\n| Function or symbol | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `TrueBool::deserialize` | `parser` | Parses success envelope booleans through a separated protocol-bool parser and `ok=true` validator. | None; behavior remains the protocol invariant. |\n| `FalseBool::deserialize` | `parser` | Parses error envelope booleans through a separated protocol-bool parser and `ok=false` validator. | None; behavior remains the protocol invariant. |\n| `deserialize_protocol_bool` | `parser` | Parses provider protocol boolean fields before invariant validation. | None. |\n| `true_bool_from_value` | `validator` | Validates `ok=true` for success envelopes. | None. |\n| `false_bool_from_value` | `validator` | Validates `ok=false` for error envelopes. | None. |\n| `ProviderConcurrency` | `mapper` | Maps provider `describe.concurrency` JSON into a typed DTO while accepting optional legacy fields and flattened provider-specific metadata. | None; DTO broadening is bounded to this protocol object. |\n| `ErrorResponseEnvelope::process_status` | `mapper` | Maps provider error envelope process status into the typed `ProcessStatus` DTO. | None; raw JSON status parsing is removed from provider settings. |\n| `fixed_str_type!::*::deserialize` | `parser` | Parses fixed-kind launch event discriminator strings via a shared fixed-string validator. | None; expected values are unchanged. |\n| `deserialize_fixed_str_type` | `validator` | Validates fixed launch event discriminator strings against the expected literal. | None. |\n| `fixed_str_type_error` | `formatter` | Formats fixed-string discriminator validation errors. | None. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ProviderCapabilityError::provider_reported_process_status` | `accessor` | Reads the typed process status reported inside the provider capability error envelope. | None; caller falls back to client process status when provider status is absent. |\n| `parse_error_response_envelope` | `parser` | Parses provider error envelopes into the typed `ErrorResponseEnvelope` DTO. | None; error parsing remains schema-bound. |\n| `schema_invalid_error_response` | `mapper` | Maps malformed provider error envelopes into the canonical schema-invalid protocol error. | None. |\n| `capability_error_from_envelope` | `mapper` | Maps a valid provider error envelope plus diagnostics/status into `ProviderCapabilityError`. | None. |\n| `missing_non_launch_envelope_result` | `mapper` | Maps missing non-launch stdout to empty-stdout or nonzero transport errors based on process status. | None. |\n| `non_launch_response_kind` | `mapper` | Maps envelope `ok` and process status into the non-launch response kind. | None. |\n| `envelope_ok` | `accessor` | Reads the optional `ok` boolean from a raw provider envelope. | None. |\n| `map_non_launch_response` | `mapper` | Maps classified non-launch envelopes into success, capability, transport, or schema-invalid results. | None. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_registry/options.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ProviderRegistryOptions::with_path_entries_from_process_path` | `accessor` | Reads the current process `PATH` and delegates to path-entry option mapping. | None; no filesystem scan occurs here. |\n| `ProviderRegistryOptions::with_path_entries_from_path_env` | `mapper` | Maps an optional PATH environment value into provider-client resolver options. | None; absent PATH remains an empty resolver list. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_settings/mod.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ProviderSettingsHostOptions::with_path_entries_from_process_path` | `mapper` | Applies process-PATH resolver entries to provider settings host options. | None; mirrors provider registry option behavior. |\n| `ProviderSettingsHost::cached_settings_target` | `accessor` | Reads a cloned settings target from the in-memory target cache. | None. |\n| `ProviderSettingsHost::load_settings_target` | `orchestration` | Loads provider describe output and maps it into a settings target on cache miss. | None. |\n| `ProviderSettingsHost::cache_settings_target` | `mapper` | Stores a cloned settings target under its model name after successful describe. | None. |\n| `settings_target_from_description` | `mapper` | Maps provider describe output into the host settings-target DTO. | None. |\n| `From<ProviderClientError> for ProviderSettingsError` | `mapper` | Maps provider capability and transport/protocol errors into provider-settings command errors, preferring typed provider-reported status over client process status. | None; preserves existing structured error fields. |\n| `provider_error_status` | `mapper` | Maps typed `ProcessStatus` variants into provider settings process-status DTOs. | None; no raw stdout parsing remains. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `build_launch_candidate` | `mapper` | Builds the launch candidate from provider config, model args, prompt inputs, cwd, and inherited env. | None; construction remains data mapping. |\n| `build_policy_request` | `mapper` | Builds `policy.evaluate` request params with provider-compatible model and launch objects. | None. |\n| `build_launch_request` | `mapper` | Builds `launch` request params with corrected model provider args and launch argv/env/stdin. | None. |\n| `provider_model_request` | `mapper` | Maps model name, prompt, named inputs, and selected model-local provider args into protocol model fields. | None. |\n| `policy_launch_object` | `mapper` | Maps provider command/base args/prompt mode and candidate launch state into policy launch metadata. | None. |\n| `model_provider_args` | `accessor` | Reads the selected pool member's model-local provider args using `provider_index`. | None. |\n| `base_provider_args` | `filter` | Removes model-local suffix args from effective launch args to expose provider base args. | Low; suffix stripping is covered by S10 launch-shape assertions. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/policy_transform.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `apply_policy_transform` | `mapper` | Applies provider policy output to a launch candidate; env entries now extend inherited env instead of replacing it. | None; behavior is covered by PATH preservation assertions. |\n| `ensure_policy_accepted` | `validator` | Rejects provider policy results that are not accepted before applying any transform. | None. |\n| `apply_accepted_policy_transform` | `mapper` | Applies accepted argv/env/stdin/prompt transforms to a launch candidate. | None. |\n| `prompt_arg_matches` | `predicate` | Answers whether an argv prompt candidate still matches the previous prompt. | None. |\n| `replace_prompt_arg` | `mapper` | Replaces the prompt argv string after the predicate passes. | None. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `launch_session_capture` | `mapper` | Maps launch session metadata into runtime session-capture method and id fields. | None. |\n| `launch_provider_session_id` | `accessor` | Reads optional LaunchExit session metadata before id extraction. | None. |\n| `provider_session_id_from_value` | `mapper` | Maps raw LaunchExit session JSON into an accepted provider session id. | None. |\n| `raw_provider_session_id` | `accessor` | Reads `session.provider_session_id`, falling back to schema-compatible `session.session_id`. | None; alias behavior is covered by the S10B regression. |\n| `accepted_provider_session_id` | `filter` | Drops empty provider session ids and returns owned accepted ids. | None. |\n| `provider_session_id_is_present` | `predicate` | Answers whether a provider session id string is non-empty. | None. |\n| `owned_provider_session_id` | `mapper` | Converts an accepted borrowed provider session id into an owned string. | None. |\n\n### `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `resolve_resume_workspace_root` | `orchestration` | Tries external session runtime cwd metadata before legacy session storage cwd. | None; positive external cwd path is covered by S10 resume integration. |\n| `external_session_runtime_workspace_root` | `orchestration` | Coordinates external-session detection, mailbox lookup, cwd extraction, and validation. | None; helpers keep validation and mapping separate. |\n| `external_session_runtime_db` | `accessor` | Opens the default mailbox sidecar if present. | None; absence is represented as `None`. |\n| `validate_external_session_runtime_cwd` | `validator` | Accepts only absolute cwd values from session runtime metadata. | Low; positive absolute path covered, rejection path not newly covered. |\n| `external_session_runtime_cwd_path` | `mapper` | Maps recorded runtime cwd strings into `PathBuf` values before validation. | None. |\n| `require_absolute_external_session_runtime_cwd` | `validator` | Validates that recorded external runtime cwd paths are absolute. | Low; positive absolute path covered, rejection path not newly covered. |\n| `external_session_runtime_cwd_is_absolute` | `predicate` | Answers whether the recorded runtime cwd path is absolute. | None. |\n| `external_session_runtime_cwd_not_absolute` | `mapper` | Maps a non-absolute external runtime cwd path into an operational metadata error. | None. |\n| `external_session_runtime_cwd_not_absolute_message` | `formatter` | Formats the non-absolute external runtime cwd error message. | None. |\n| `external_session_runtime_error` | `mapper` | Maps mailbox errors into `MetadataError`. | None. |\n\n### `src-tauri/src/commands/provider_settings.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `package_migration_legacy_payload` | `orchestration` | Coordinates model and providers TOML packaging for provider settings migration. | None. |\n| `packaged_provider_blocks` | `orchestration` | Loads configured provider blocks and reads the providers TOML JSON payload. | None. |\n| `providers_toml_path` | `accessor` | Computes the sibling `providers.toml` path for the models directory. | None. |\n| `read_provider_blocks` | `orchestration` | Reads provider blocks when the TOML file exists, otherwise returns an empty provider map. | None. |\n| `provider_blocks_file_exists` | `predicate` | Answers whether the providers TOML file exists. | None. |\n| `empty_provider_blocks` | `mapper` | Produces an empty providers JSON object for missing providers TOML. | None. |\n| `read_toml_text` | `accessor` | Reads TOML file text and maps IO failure into command error DTOs. | None. |\n| `parse_toml_value` | `parser` | Parses TOML text into a TOML value for migration payload packaging. | None. |\n| `toml_json_value` | `mapper` | Maps parsed TOML values into JSON command payloads. | None. |\n| `settings_host_lock_error` | `mapper` | Maps poisoned settings-host lock errors into provider settings error DTOs. | None. |\n| `transport_error_dto` | `mapper` | Builds test-double transport error DTOs for provider settings command harness failures. | None; test harness only. |\n| `test_update_error` | `accessor` | Reads an optional update error from the provider settings command test double. | None; test harness only. |\n| `test_validate_error` | `accessor` | Reads an optional validate error from the provider settings command test double. | None; test harness only. |\n| `command_error_result` | `mapper` | Wraps provider settings test-double errors into command results. | None; test harness only. |\n\n### `src-tauri/src/run/balancing/finalization.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ingest_completed_attempt_session` | `orchestration` | Adds external session runtime recording to completed attempt finalization. | None; non-fatal record path is isolated. |\n| `record_external_session_runtime_if_needed` | `orchestration` | Gates runtime-cwd recording to external-provider sessions with a known session id. | None. |\n| `external_runtime_session_id` | `accessor` | Selects the external session id from zero-turn or captured provider session data. | None. |\n| `record_external_session_runtime` | `orchestration` | Opens mailbox metadata storage and records `session_runtime.effective_cwd`. | Low; failure is warning-only by design. |\n\n### `src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs`\n\n| Function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `run_resume_attempt` | `orchestration` | Coordinates provider-ref-aware resume strategy selection and attempt execution. | None. |\n| `resume_attempt_strategy_for_target` | `orchestration` | Allows provider-ref models to bypass legacy resume strategy requirements. | None. |\n| `execute_resume_attempt_command` | `orchestration` | Chooses external provider executor request for provider-ref resumes, otherwise legacy CLI resume. | None; branch is covered by S10 resume integration. |\n| `provider_ref_resume_executor_request` | `mapper` | Builds `EffectiveWithStartKnownProviderSessionId` executor request for provider-ref resume. | None. |\n| `prepare_initial_headless_resume_target` | `orchestration` | Passes resolved resume metadata into provider-ref-aware validation. | None. |\n| `validate_headless_resume_target` | `validator` | Accepts provider-ref resume targets without a legacy provider `resume` block only after provider-ref target validation. | None. |\n| `validate_provider_ref_headless_resume_target` | `validator` | Validates resolved model/provider-ref presence, provider index bounds, and selected-provider identity before provider-ref resume bypass. | None; fail-closed before bypass/migration skip. |\n| `provider_ref_resolved_model` | `accessor` | Reads the optional resolved model config from a resume target. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_model_has_implementation` | `predicate` | Answers whether the resolved model has a root provider implementation reference. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_target_member_name` | `accessor` | Reads the selected provider member name by provider index. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_loaded_provider_name` | `accessor` | Reads the loaded provider name from the resume execution target. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_missing_model_message` | `formatter` | Formats provider-ref resume validation failure for missing model config. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_missing_implementation_message` | `formatter` | Formats provider-ref resume validation failure for missing implementation reference. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_invalid_index_message` | `formatter` | Formats provider-ref resume validation failure for invalid provider index. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_resolved_provider_message` | `formatter` | Formats provider-ref resume validation failure for resolved-provider mismatch. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_loaded_provider_message` | `formatter` | Formats provider-ref resume validation failure for loaded-provider mismatch. | None. |\n| `provider_ref_resume_block_exit_code` | `formatter` | Emits a provider-ref resume validation failure and returns the canonical headless failure exit code. | None. |\n| `migrate_resume_target` | `orchestration` | Skips default legacy migration for provider-ref resumes unless manual migration is requested, after provider-ref target validation. | None. |\n| `should_skip_provider_ref_default_migration` | `predicate` | Answers whether provider-ref resume should skip default migration. | None. |\n| `resolved_uses_provider_ref` | `predicate` | Detects whether the resolved model has a root provider implementation reference. | None. |\n\n### Tauri registry wiring constructors\n\n| File and function | A1 class | Meaning | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src-tauri/src/app_state.rs::provider_registry_options` | `mapper` | Builds GUI provider registry options with config/data roots and process `PATH`. | None. |\n| `src-tauri/src/commands/provider_settings.rs::host_options` | `mapper` | Builds provider settings host options with config/data roots and process `PATH`. | None. |\n| `src-tauri/src/commands/session_locate_export/orchestration.rs::build_session_locate_provider_registry` | `orchestration` | Builds locate/export provider registry options with process `PATH`. | None. |\n| `src-tauri/src/wiring.rs::AgentRuntimeServices::cli_defaults` | `orchestration` | Builds CLI default services with PATH-aware provider registry. | None. |\n| `src-tauri/src/wiring.rs::AgentRuntimeServices::production` | `orchestration` | Builds production services with PATH-aware provider registry. | None. |\n\n## Test function inventory\n\nOnly added or meaningfully changed tests and fixture helpers are listed.\n\n| File | Function | A1 class | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs` | `invoke_describe_accepts_schema_valid_freeform_concurrency_metadata` | `validator` | Proves provider describe accepts schema-valid free-form concurrency metadata. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs` | `binary_ref_resolves_from_process_path_entries` | `validator` | Proves binary provider refs resolve through supplied process PATH entries. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs` | `absent_binary_from_process_path_entries_preserves_missing_artifact` | `validator` | Proves missing binaries remain `missing_artifact`. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs` | `unset_process_path_entries_preserves_missing_artifact_without_panic` | `validator` | Proves unset PATH is safe and non-resolving. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_settings_host.rs` | `settings_host_preserves_conflict_error_details_and_diagnostics` | `validator` | Proves provider settings preserves provider capability details, diagnostics, and typed process status. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/s10_external_launch_session.rs` | `external_launch_exit_session_populates_capture_and_resume_request` | `validator` | Proves protocol shape, PATH preservation, launch session capture, and known-session relaunch. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/age244_s7b_production_wiring_source_guard.rs` | `s10_production_provider_registries_populate_path_entries_from_process_path` | `validator` | Proves production registry constructors opt into process PATH entries. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `external_provider_resume_without_rotate_uses_external_launch_and_recorded_cwd` | `validator` | Proves launch+resume through external provider path, recorded cwd, no rotation/migration, and persisted rows. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `external_launch_session_id_alias_persists_external_capture_method_without_session_capability` | `validator` | Proves `session_id` alias persists `external_provider_launch` capture without session capability. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs` | `session_external_provider_source_paths`, `source_entry_path`, `read_session_external_provider_source` | `mapper`, `accessor` | Keep production source-guard traversal separated from source path mapping and reads. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_settings_host.rs` | `recorded_calls`, `recorded_calls_text`, `parse_recorded_calls`, `parse_recorded_call`, `recorded_call_is_for_provider`, `recorded_call_subcommand` | `parser`, `filter`, `mapper` | Keep recorded provider-call fixture parsing/filtering separated from settings assertions. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/age244_s7b_production_wiring_source_guard.rs` | `source_marker_index`, `source_end_marker_index`, `source_slice_between`, `compact_source_and_needle`, `assert_compact_absent` | `accessor`, `mapper`, `validator` | Keep source-slice and compact-whitespace guard helpers separated from assertions. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `fixture_paths`, `create_fixture_directories`, `write_model_config`, `model_config_toml`, `write_providers_config`, `providers_config_toml`, `fixture_from_paths` | `mapper`, `formatter` | Materialize isolated S10 launch/resume configs and fixture paths. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `invocation_session_row`, `provider_record_text`, `parse_provider_records`, `provider_record_line_has_content`, `parse_provider_record` | `parser`, `filter`, `mapper` | Read and parse invocation rows plus provider request JSONL records. |\n| `src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs` | `provider_record_subcommands`, `provider_record_subcommand`, `assert_no_forbidden_provider_subcommands`, `provider_subcommand_is_allowed` | `accessor`, `validator`, `predicate` | Verify the external resume path did not invoke rotation, migration, or legacy resume subcommands. |\n\n## Adapter declarations\n\n```yaml\nadapter_declarations:\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs\n    role: adapter\n    Translates:\n      - external provider JSON protocol envelopes\n      - Oulipoly typed provider client DTOs\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs\n    role: adapter\n    Translates:\n      - Oulipoly model/provider dispatch context\n      - external provider policy.evaluate and launch request JSON contracts\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs\n    role: adapter\n    Translates:\n      - external provider LaunchExit event stream/session metadata\n      - Oulipoly runtime execution result and session capture fields\n  - component: src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs\n    role: adapter\n    Translates:\n      - Oulipoly resolved resume targets\n      - external provider start-known-session launch requests\n      - legacy CLI resume requests when no provider ref is present\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs\n    role: adapter\n    Translates:\n      - mailbox session_runtime metadata\n      - resume workspace root decisions\n```\n\n## Intrinsic-surface declarations\n\n```yaml\nintrinsic_surface_declarations:\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/provider_registry/options.rs\n    role: intrinsic-surface\n    Domain: provider_artifact_resolution_options\n    Owns:\n      - process PATH entry capture for binary provider refs\n      - absent PATH handling as an empty resolver entry set\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/session_metadata/mod.rs\n    role: intrinsic-surface\n    Domain: external_session_runtime_workspace_root\n    Owns:\n      - session_runtime.effective_cwd lookup\n      - absolute-path validation for recorded external runtime cwd\n  - component: src-tauri/src/run/balancing/finalization.rs\n    role: intrinsic-surface\n    Domain: external_session_runtime_recording\n    Owns:\n      - non-fatal recording of external provider session runtime cwd\n```\n\nNo other intrinsic surfaces are declared for this gate.\n\n## Test-harness declarations\n\n```yaml\ntest_harness_declarations:\n  - component: src-tauri/tests/s10_external_provider_resume.rs\n    role: test-harness\n    Surface:\n      - isolated XDG config/data/cache fixture directories\n      - external provider Python script fixture\n      - CLI launch and resume command execution\n      - provider request JSONL recording\n      - state.db invocation row assertions through rusqlite\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/s10_external_launch_session.rs\n    role: test-harness\n    Surface:\n      - external provider executor service fixture\n      - policy.evaluate and launch request capture\n      - LaunchExit session capture assertions\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/provider_registry.rs\n    role: test-harness\n    Surface:\n      - provider artifact registry fixture\n      - temporary PATH and executable binary fixture\n      - missing artifact diagnostics\n  - component: crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs\n    role: test-harness\n    Surface:\n      - provider client subprocess fixture\n      - describe response JSON compatibility assertions\n```\n\nNo `state.db` schema migration is declared or required by this gate.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":307,"totalLines":307,"truncated":false}},"title":"planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md","time":{"start":1780750073958,"end":1780750074030}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a3a67d3acdf6d8b016a2416f9d5ac8196bead1df88524b439"}},"id":"prt_e9cf9c05d001oEMtdvO3nnpXyz","sessionID":"ses_1630698a4ffe6jRHOZ2eUQGXQ5","messageID":"msg_e9cf996d4001LC0tzd2Tfly5HJ"}}
